
$ helm repo add headlamp https://kubernetes-sigs.github.io/headlamp/
"headlamp" already exists with the same configuration, skipping

$ helm repo update headlamp
Hang tight while we grab the latest from your chart repositories...
...Successfully got an update from the "headlamp" chart repository
Update Complete. ⎈Happy Helming!⎈

$ helm upgrade --install my-headlamp headlamp/headlamp --namespace kube-system --wait
Release "my-headlamp" does not exist. Installing it now.
NAME: my-headlamp
LAST DEPLOYED: Tue Nov 24 02:14:50 2026
NAMESPACE: kube-system
STATUS: deployed
REVISION: 1
DESCRIPTION: Install complete
TEST SUITE: None
NOTES:
1. Get the application URL by running these commands:
  export POD_NAME=$(kubectl get pods --namespace kube-system -l "app.kubernetes.io/name=headlamp,app.kubernetes.io/instance=my-headlamp" -o jsonpath="{.items[0].metadata.name}")
  export CONTAINER_PORT=$(kubectl get pod --namespace kube-system $POD_NAME -o jsonpath="{.spec.containers[0].ports[0].containerPort}")
  echo "Visit http://127.0.0.1:8080 to use your application"
  kubectl --namespace kube-system port-forward $POD_NAME 8080:$CONTAINER_PORT
2. Get the token using
  kubectl create token my-headlamp --namespace kube-system

$ kubectl get deployment,service my-headlamp --namespace kube-system
NAME                          READY   UP-TO-DATE   AVAILABLE   AGE
deployment.apps/my-headlamp   1/1     1            1           7s

NAME                  TYPE        CLUSTER-IP    EXTERNAL-IP   PORT(S)   AGE
service/my-headlamp   ClusterIP   10.96.8.184   <none>        80/TCP    7s

$ kubectl apply -f admin-user.yaml -f viewer-user.yaml
serviceaccount/admin-user created
clusterrolebinding.rbac.authorization.k8s.io/admin-user created
serviceaccount/viewer-user created
clusterrolebinding.rbac.authorization.k8s.io/viewer-user created

$ kubectl create token admin-user --namespace kube-system --duration=1h | cut -c1-40; echo '...'
eyJhbGciOiJSUzI1NiIsImtpZCI6IkkwZ2Q5NXAz
...

$ kubectl auth can-i delete pods --all-namespaces --as=system:serviceaccount:kube-system:admin-user
yes

$ kubectl auth can-i list pods --all-namespaces --as=system:serviceaccount:kube-system:viewer-user
yes

$ kubectl auth can-i delete pods --all-namespaces --as=system:serviceaccount:kube-system:viewer-user || true
no

$ kubectl auth can-i get secrets --namespace default --as=system:serviceaccount:kube-system:viewer-user || true
no

Apri Headlamp con:  kubectl port-forward --namespace kube-system svc/my-headlamp 4466:80   -> http://localhost:4466
e usa il token di admin-user (kubectl create token admin-user -n kube-system) oppure di viewer-user.
